  name "the-object-of-a-field-read-past-a-possible-absence"
  note "A dot after `?.` or after `?[` reads a field of the declared struct the walk reached past the absence, so its step stands at the field's place with the mark riding on it, as a dot after a plain segment does. `p?.y`, `xs?[0].y` and `q.y` each read `y` at place 1, and none by the name a value whose type a call decides is read by."
